<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acts of the Apostles</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Acts of the Apostles is the fifth book of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-testament">New Testament</a>, written by the author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospel-of-luke">Gospel of Luke</a>, probably late in the 1st century CE. It tells of the early Christian community in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the missions of Peter and Paul across the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. It records that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i">Herod Agrippa I</a> had the apostle James executed and describes Agrippa's sudden death at Caesarea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/acts-of-the-apostles.jpg" alt="Acts of the Apostles" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berlin,_Staatliche_Museen_zu_Berlin_MS_Uncial_8683_verso_Acts_5,_12%E2%80%9321.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
